	quest_links: [ ]
	quests: [
		{
			dependencies: ["6C0C75598D65CE7D"]
			description: [
				"&6The Space Program&r. Your island floats in the void - but there is a whole SOLAR SYSTEM out there to conquer."
				""
				"Ad Astra takes you off-world: the Moon, Mars, Venus, Mercury, and the frozen exoplanet Glacio. Each needs a bigger rocket and better gear to survive."
				""
				"&a&lNothing has to die for this.&r Space is gated by &lwork&r, not by combat - steel, oil, oxygen and a launch pad. Build the rocket and go."
				""
				"&e&lWhat is actually out there:&r"
				"&7- &fThe Moon&7 - &eDesh&7. This is the big one: the AE2 ME Controller is built from it, so your first real storage network starts here."
				"&7- &fMars&7 - &eOstrum&7. AE2 autocrafting, Advanced Computers, and the Blue Skies lighter."
				"&7- &fVenus&7 - &eCalorite&7. Spatial storage and MEGA cells."
				""
				"&8Mercury and Glacio have no gate hanging off them - they are there because they are there."
			]
			icon: "ad_astra:tier_1_rocket"
			id: "0C5265A68B7CA881"
			rewards: [
				{
					id: "0C79A18F0811CA50"
					type: "xp"
					xp: 50
				}
				{
					id: "386D6C4984D7B09E"
					type: "random"
				}
			]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.5d
			subtitle: "&7Leave the atmosphere"
			tasks: [{
				id: "12B64518BFDE5C15"
				title: "Begin the Space Program"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "&9Reach for the Stars"
			x: -9.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["0C5265A68B7CA881"]
			description: [
				"Ad Astra runs on its own Steel. Build a &eCompressor&r and press iron plates and steel - the base of every rocket and machine."
				""
				"&c&lAd Astra Steel is not Mekanism Steel.&r They are separate items with separate recipes, and the rocket recipes want this one specifically. Do not assume your Mekanism stockpile covers it."
				""
				"&e&lThe Compressor is the workhorse of this chapter.&r Everything above is plates - iron plates, desh plates, ostrum plates, calorite plates - and every one of them comes from here. Build it early and feed it constantly."
				""
				"&e&lThe machine order that saves you time:&r"
				"&71.&r &7Compressor&r - plates, the universal input"
				"&72.&r &7NASA Workbench&r - assembles rockets"
				"&73.&r &7Fuel Refinery&r + &7Oxygen Loader&r - the consumables"
				"&74.&r &7Launch Pad&r - and you are flying"
				""
				"&7All of them take Forge Energy, so wire this area into your main grid rather than running a dedicated generator.&r"
				""
				"&8Press far more plates than the first rocket needs. Every tier above uses the same machine and you will be back here four times."
			]
			icon: "ad_astra:compressor"
			id: "025F9F5BB50F3C61"
			rewards: [{
				id: "35BE749B6A52C973"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 20
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Everything above starts here"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "44F847626F40F02C"
					item: "ad_astra:compressor"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					count: 8L
					id: "558E3813BF30604D"
					item: "ad_astra:steel_ingot"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&9Aerospace Steel"
			x: -7.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["025F9F5BB50F3C61"]
			description: [
				"A &6Coal Generator&r burns coal for FE. Crude, cheap, and it works on day one."
				""
				"&e&lYou do not have to use it.&r Every Ad Astra machine takes FE from anything - Create, Mekanism, Thermal, the Power Grid. If you already have generation, wire it in and skip the coal entirely."
				""
				"&7The &6Energizer&7 used to sit in this quest. It is built from &eostrum&7, so it is not craftable until Mars - it now has its own quest out on the Red Frontier.&r"
			]
			icon: "ad_astra:coal_generator"
			id: "1654EA4BC9A74F79"
			rewards: [{
				id: "1B3A4C9D6BD278BA"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 20
			}]
			subtitle: "&7The pad needs feeding"
			tasks: [{
				id: "27C8645AB9E76C60"
				item: "ad_astra:coal_generator"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Ground Power"
			x: -7.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["025F9F5BB50F3C61"]
			description: [
				"The &bOxygen Loader&r fills tanks and suits. It is plain steel, so you can build it before you ever leave the ground - which is the point, because you cannot reach the Moon without oxygen."
				""
				"&e&lThat is all you need for the trip.&r Loader, a tank, and a space suit."
				""
				"&7The &bOxygen Distributor&7 and &bWater Pump&7 are base-building blocks rather than travel gear, and both are framed in &edesh&7 - so they wait until you have stood on the Moon. See &fLife Support&7.&r"
			]
			icon: "ad_astra:oxygen_loader"
			id: "15008CDD6EC8DA95"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7C51C336ACD0DF08"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Oxygen or nothing"
			tasks: [{
				id: "23647E2660285C01"
				item: "ad_astra:oxygen_loader"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&9Something to Breathe"
			x: -7.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["025F9F5BB50F3C61"]
			description: [
				"Rockets run on refined Fuel, and Fuel comes from Oil - but &cno oil wells survive in a void world&r."
				""
				"So you make your own: &e8 Coal Blocks around a Bucket = Crude Oil&r. Feed it to the Fuel Refinery and fill your tanks. Your HNN and essence farms will keep the coal flowing."
			]
			icon: "ad_astra:fuel_refinery"
			id: "4E40677713DCB756"
			rewards: [{
				id: "176544BA4BEA02CC"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Refine it before you burn it"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "203263A724E0B1B6"
					item: "ad_astra:fuel_refinery"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "724D9773DC100961"
					item: "ad_astra:fuel_bucket"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&9Fuel the Fire"
			x: -7.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["15008CDD6EC8DA95"]
			description: [
				"A full Space Suit - helmet, suit, pants, boots - keeps you alive off-world. Fill its tanks at the &eOxygen Loader&r before every trip."
				""
				"&c&lAll four pieces, or it does not work.&r A partial suit provides no oxygen at all. This is the single most common way people die on their first launch."
				""
				"&e&lOxygen is consumed continuously while off-world.&r The tank empties whether you are mining or standing still. Check it before you launch, and carry a spare filled tank for anything longer than a quick survey."
				""
				"&e&lThe upgrade path:&r"
				"&7- &fSpace Suit&7 - Moon and Mars"
				"&7- &fNetherite Space Suit&7 - required in practice for &cVenus&7, where acid rain eats the basic suit"
				""
				"&e&lOxygen Distributor&r is the other half of the answer. Placed in a sealed room with power and oxygen, it fills the space with breathable air - so you can take the helmet off, eat, and build a real base rather than living on tank time."
				""
				"&8Build the Oxygen Loader before the rocket. Arriving on the Moon with empty tanks is a very short expedition."
			]
			icon: {
				Count: 1
				id: "ad_astra:space_suit"
				tag: {
					Damage: 0
				}
			}
