		}
		{
			dependencies: ["6790D53BA13D38CC"]
			description: [
				"One small step. The Moon: low gravity, no air, hostile nights - and &eDesh&r ore, the metal of every rocket above Tier 1."
				""
				"&6&lThis single landing unlocks two entire systems.&r"
				"&7- &bAE2 autocrafting&7 - Molecular Assemblers and Crafting CPUs are framed in Desh. Storage worked without it; crafting does not."
				"&7- &aThe Undergarden&7 - its catalyst is cored with &eDesh&7, so the Moon is what opens it."
				""
				"&c&lYou are the reason it is gated this way.&r Nothing else in the pack forces you off the island. This does."
				""
				"&e&lWhat to bring:&r a full Space Suit with loaded oxygen, food, blocks, and a &7Oxygen Distributor&r if you plan to stay. Low gravity makes jumps enormous - it is easy to launch yourself somewhere you cannot get back from."
				""
				"&e&lWhat to bring home:&r &lfar more Desh than you think.&r Every Crafting CPU and every Molecular Assembler wants it, and you will want several of both. A stack is a sensible first haul, not four ingots."
				""
				"&7Set up a Mekanism Teleporter or a Quantum Entangloporter here on your first trip. Doing so means you never build a return rocket again.&r"
			]
			icon: "ad_astra:moon_sand"
			id: "75B7246A1B0C350B"
			rewards: [{
				count: 6
				id: "2F45558CC5C2B69F"
				item: "ad_astra:raw_desh"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Desh, the ME Controller and the Undergarden"
			tasks: [{
				dimension: "ad_astra:moon"
				id: "66D267109143739F"
				type: "dimension"
			}]
			title: "&9The Moon"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["75B7246A1B0C350B"]
			description: [
				"Smelt Desh and build a &eTier 2 Rocket&r - enough thrust to cross to the inner planets."
				""
				"&6&lThis is the quest where AE2 autocrafting unlocks.&r Desh is not just rocket fuel-metal - it frames the &bMolecular Assembler&r and the &bCrafting CPU&r. Bring enough home and you can finally stop hand-crafting."
				""
				"&e&lRockets are consumed on launch&r - you do not get the ship back. Every trip costs a full rocket plus fuel, which is why a Mekanism Teleporter or Quantum Entangloporter on the destination pays for itself almost immediately."
				""
				"&e&lRocket tiers and where they reach:&r"
				"&7- &fTier 1&7 - the Moon"
				"&7- &fTier 2&7 - Mars"
				"&7- &fTier 3&7 - Venus, Mercury"
				"&7- &fTier 4&7 - Glacio"
				""
				"&7Build it on the Launch Pad with the NASA Workbench, fuel it, then right-click to board and press space to launch.&r"
				""
				"&8Take building blocks, food, and a spare oxygen tank on every flight. Arriving somewhere hostile with an empty inventory is how first trips end badly."
			]
			icon: "ad_astra:desh_ingot"
			id: "5954D67B54D46F03"
			rewards: [{
				id: "20DF2D652B4717D2"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 40
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Moon metal - and AE2 autocrafting"
			tasks: [
				{
					count: 4L
					id: "611EE4680750D69B"
					item: "ad_astra:desh_ingot"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "26AEB3BD5D638AF4"
					item: "ad_astra:tier_2_rocket"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&9Desh & Tier 2"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5954D67B54D46F03"]
			description: [
				"Mars: the red frontier. &eOstrum&r ore, ruined structures, and hostile Martian raiders. Watch your oxygen."
				""
				"&6&lMars is the computer gate.&r Ostrum now frames both the &bAdvanced Computer&r and the &bPeripheral Casing&r - and since every Advanced Peripherals block is built on that casing, this planet unlocks the whole computer-automation layer in one trip."
				""
				"&e&lIt also opens the Undergarden&r - that dimension's catalyst is cored with Mars ostrum."
				""
				"&e&lWhat is different from the Moon:&r there are hostile mobs here that will actually fight you, and ruined structures worth looting. Gravity is higher than the Moon but still low. Oxygen is still mandatory."
				""
				"&7Bring a weapon this time. The Moon was empty; Mars is not.&r"
				""
				"&e&lWhat to bring home:&r Ostrum in quantity. One ingot per Advanced Computer sounds cheap until you are building a monitor wall and a dozen peripherals."
				""
				"&8Mystical Agriculture has ostrum seeds - but you need the ingot first to craft them. Bring enough home to start that farm and you never mine Mars again."
			]
			icon: "ad_astra:mars_sand"
			id: "7AEFF5201E41906E"
			rewards: [{
				count: 6
				id: "359DA50EBEA3BE77"
				item: "ad_astra:raw_ostrum"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Mars, and the computer gate"
			tasks: [{
				dimension: "ad_astra:mars"
				id: "0D06BDC09913AB26"
				type: "dimension"
			}]
			title: "&9Red Frontier"
			x: 4.0d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7AEFF5201E41906E"]
			description: [
				"&6Ostrum&r from Mars, and the &6Tier 3 Rocket&r it builds."
				""
				"&e&lTier 3 opens the harsh worlds&r - Venus and Mercury. Both will kill an under-equipped player quickly, so this is the point where the space suit stops being optional."
				""
				"&7Ostrum also gates AE2 autocrafting, Advanced Computers and the Blue Skies lighter, so you will be back for more of it regardless.&r"
			]
			icon: "ad_astra:ostrum_ingot"
			id: "5B3D9DD3AF77FB22"
			rewards: [{
				id: "2755C2C2DF6519A9"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 40
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Mars metal - computers unlock"
			tasks: [
				{
					count: 4L
					id: "0D900B8726F91858"
					item: "ad_astra:ostrum_ingot"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "304DDE23F9A0C494"
					item: "ad_astra:tier_3_rocket"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&9Ostrum & Tier 3"
			x: 6.0d
			y: -1.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5B3D9DD3AF77FB22"]
			description: [
				"Venus: crushing pressure, acid rain, and &eCalorite&r ore. A Netherite Space Suit is strongly advised."
				""
				"&6&lVenus is the endgame-storage gate.&r Calorite now frames the &bSpatial IO Port&r and &bSky Steel&r - and Sky Steel is the base of every single MEGA Cell. If you want storage beyond stock AE2, it is on this planet."
				""
				"&e&lIt also lights the Everbright&r - the Blue Skies zeal lighter is forged from Venus calorite."
				""
				"&c&lThis is the first genuinely lethal world.&r Acid rain damages you through an ordinary space suit. The &7Netherite Space Suit&r is not a luxury here - upgrade before you land, not after."
				""
				"&7Build shelter immediately on arrival. An Oxygen Distributor inside a sealed room turns Venus from a countdown into a base.&r"
				""
				"&e&lWhat to bring home:&r Calorite, and plenty. Between Spatial Storage and the MEGA cell line you will consume more of this than of Desh or Ostrum."
				""
				"&8Also a Celestial Core ingredient - one Calorite ingot goes into the item that ends the pack."
			]
			icon: "ad_astra:venus_sand"
			id: "45A0F1081A90EE29"
			rewards: [{
				count: 6
				id: "3C401C618966A48A"
				item: "ad_astra:raw_calorite"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Venus: acid rain and heat"
			tasks: [{
				dimension: "ad_astra:venus"
				id: "3AE534BE40559A80"
				type: "dimension"
			}]
			title: "&9Hell's Frontier"
			x: 8.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5B3D9DD3AF77FB22"]
			description: [
				"&cMercury&r - scorched, airless, and the closest world to the sun."
				""
				"&e&lNo atmosphere at all&r, so oxygen is not optional for a second, and the day side will cook an unprotected player."
				""
				"&7There is no gate hanging off Mercury. It is here because it is here - a flag to plant and a hostile rock to survive.&r"
			]
			icon: "ad_astra:venus_sand"
			id: "6B7764A7A361338F"
			rewards: [{
				id: "1F5F5432A6B846C7"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 40
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Nothing here wants you alive"
			tasks: [{
				dimension: "ad_astra:mercury"
